 r←Test_CheckVersions_005(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;old;new;qdmx;rc;msg
⍝ `CheckForDowngrades` must refuse to replace an installed package by an earlier version of it.\\
⍝ That is what an update does to a version that was withdrawn from the Registry it came from, or
⍝ that was never published: `ReInstallDependencies_` widens the exact version to its major version
⍝ line, and the best version of that line is then older than what is installed. Because the install
⍝ folder is afterwards swapped for the temporary one, the only copy there is would be gone.\\
⍝ Needs no Registry: the function compares two build lists and nothing else.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 old←∆GetTempDir'old'
 new←∆GetTempDir'new'

⍝ Installed a beta, Registry offers an earlier release: this must be refused
 (⊂∆BuildList'aplteam-APLGit2-1.2.0-beta-2')⎕NPUT(old,'/',Reg.BuildListFilename)1
 (⊂∆BuildList'aplteam-APLGit2-1.1.0')⎕NPUT(new,'/',Reg.BuildListFilename)1
 :Trap ##.Registry.ErrorNo
     old TC.CheckForDowngrades new
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'aplteam-APLGit2-1.1.0'⍷qdmx.EM
 :EndTrap

⍝ The other way round is an ordinary update and must be let through
 (⊂∆BuildList'aplteam-APLGit2-1.1.0')⎕NPUT(old,'/',Reg.BuildListFilename)1
 (⊂∆BuildList'aplteam-APLGit2-1.2.0-beta-2')⎕NPUT(new,'/',Reg.BuildListFilename)1
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≢old TC.CheckForDowngrades new

⍝ A later major version replaces nothing: the old line has no counterpart in the new build list
 (⊂∆BuildList'aplteam-APLGit2-1.2.0')⎕NPUT(old,'/',Reg.BuildListFilename)1
 (⊂∆BuildList'aplteam-APLGit2-2.0.0')⎕NPUT(new,'/',Reg.BuildListFilename)1
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≢old TC.CheckForDowngrades new

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce old
 msg Assert rc=0
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce new
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
